  {
   "id": "five-nights-at-freddy-s-help-wanted-2-250627@patch-2023-12-19",
   "gameId": "five-nights-at-freddy-s-help-wanted-2-250627",
   "displayName": "12/19/23 Rapid Patch Details",
   "kind": "patch",
   "kindBasis": "studio",
   "announcedAt": "2023-12-19T19:54:57.000Z",
   "notes": [
    {
     "title": "Changes",
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Hey folks!",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "We have just released a patch containing three, very specific fixes.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "First, players should no longer run into broken/blank cards while playing Endo Warehouse in a language other than English.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "Second, for our PC players, we’ve added a short term fix to resolve an issue where PC players are getting stuck on the EULA because controller inputs are not working. We have also added baseline support for Steam Link (Not to be confused with SteamVR, which was already supported.) We still STRONGLY recommend that you play with your headset hard wired to your PC.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": true,
       "category": "other",
       "platforms": [
        "pc"
       ]
      },
      {
       "text": "For those not able to get past the EULA, when you launch the game you will be able to enter normally and start playing, but it is far from a perfect fix. Depending on your hardware configuration, you will likely still need to rebind some inputs using SteamVR. For example, on a normal Vive, you will still need to bind your left movement stick in order to teleport.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "After investigating what we can do to add more robust support for older hardware, it became clear a stop-gap solution was our only immediate path forward, even as a partial fix. A more permanent, complete fix is now in development, but we are choosing not to rush it because it will require a considerable amount of testing.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "For players who have not run into this problem, nothing will change for you and you will be able to continue as you were.",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      },
      {
       "text": "Steel Wool Studios",
       "ps5ProOnly": false,
       "pcOnly": false,
       "category": "other"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
